/-!
# Polynomial data of the `μ > 0` passing guiding-centre field (generated)

Extra polynomial leaves in `(u, z, c, s)` for the flow form of the passing guiding-centre field
`B̃ = B + ∇×(ρ(x) b)`, `ρ(x) = ρ₀ √(1 − λ|B(x)|)`, of the rational stellarator
(`Design/RationalStellaratorGCMuFlow`), where `|B|` enters as an expression tree with two
inverse-square-root nodes:

* `P₄`, the Taylor polynomial of `R^{−4}`, and the deviation `E₄ = R⁸ P₄² − 1`, so that
  `G = P₄ (1 + E₄)^{−1/2} = R^{−4}` (a node in `u` only, majorant `≈ 4 × 10⁻³` on the tori);
* `Q P P₄ = q P P₄` (expanded), so that
  `|B| = √q R^{−4} = (q P P₄) · (1 + E)^{−1/2} (1 + E₄)^{−1/2}`
  with the node `(1 + E)^{−1/2}` of `Design/RationalStellaratorGCFlow`; the expanded product keeps
  the majorant of `|B|` small (`≈ 1.9` on the tori, against `≈ 28` for the unexpanded product);
* the partial derivatives `∂_u E₄`, `∂_u (q P P₄)`, `∂_z (q P P₄)` used by the low-resolution
  certificate.

Generated by `scripts/gc_kam/lam_gen_poly.py` (untrusted); every identity below is checked by `ring`
after pointwise evaluation.

**Sanity.** `P4P_zero`: `P₄(0) = 1`; `E4P_zero`: `E₄(0) = 0`.
-/

@[expose] public section
noncomputable section

namespace PlasmaLean.Design.RationalStellaratorGC

